  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Intermon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this Big Idea is to design a multi-country program on the intersections of climate, conflict and fragility, which will have two strong connected components: innovative footprint work which has demonstrative value and provides facts, legitimacy to the related (national and international) influencing work.

Secondly, the Big Idea seeks to contribute to an approach that brings together Oxfam&#x2019;s work in geographical areas that are impacted by the climate and conflict nexus. Several activities are planned to achieve both these objectives. A scoping study providing analytical framework and best practices, will be developed as well asa thorough donor mapping, conflict and climate sensitive assessments and implementation of identifiedpilot activities will take place in at least two sub-Saharan countries. The overall output is a well-designed concept note and programme document, accompanied by a briefing note with findings that can be used for (inter)national lobby and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Interm&#xf3;n is since 1997 a member of the international Oxfam confederation, sharing values and a strategic plan to achieve greater global impact. Interm&#xf3;n Oxfam fights, with and for disadvantaged populations and as part of a broad global movement, with the aim of eradicating injustice and poverty, and to ensure that all human beings can fully exercise their rights and enjoy a dignified life.
Mission, Vision and Values are the components of Oxfam Interm&#xf3;n identity and guide its steps as an organisation and the ideal with which Oxfam Interm&#xf3;n  wants to live in order to obtain a fairer world with greater solidarity.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
  </participating-org>
